<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49338" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tryphon</span></b> , ōnis, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A surgeon</i>, <i><span class="en">Cels. 6,
			5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7</span></i>
			praef.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A king in Syria</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 36,
				1, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">38, 9,
			3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">39, 1,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A surname of Ptolemy Philopator</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 7, 56,
				57, § 208</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>A publisher of Rome</i>, <i><span class="en">Quint.
				ad Tryph. 1</span></i> sqq.; <i><span class="en">Mart. 4,
				72, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">13, 3,
			4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
